      "mergeID": "67a9c3ebf1857c087900e94d",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Reviving an old post: https://feedback.vrchat.com/udon/p/floating-origin\n\nWould like support for floating origin to be able to create large world maps.\n\nCurrent solutions are really hacky by using stations:\n\nhttps://github.com/KitKat4191/JetSim-FloatingOrigin\n\nhttps://github.com/zhakamizhako/VRCOpenWorldMovementLogic\n\nMy suggestion is to allow us to parent the local player game object to a game object that we control so that we can control the floating origin of the player. Either by giving us direct access to the game object or have the VRCPlayerAPI have a function to parent the game object to one of our choosing.\n\nAnother suggestion would be that VRChat implement their own solution to the floating origin on server side so that all players are synced.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Floating Origin Request",
